# Local build variables. Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and never leaves your machine. The npm scripts load it
# with Node's own `--env-file-if-exists`, so a missing file is a no-op and the
# Cloudflare Pages build — which has no `.env` and gets these from its own
# build-variable settings instead — is unaffected.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Odoo Recruitment — the open vacancies on /jobs/ (build/lib/odoo-jobs.mjs)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Without them the build reads the public jobs page, which works and
# needs no credentials; with them it uses the external API, which is stable
# across Odoo's own theme changes and reads the real `is_published` flag.
#
# The key belongs to a user with read access to Recruitment and nothing more:
# an Odoo API key carries the full rights of the user it was made for. Generate
# it while logged in as that user, under My Profile -> Account Security.
#
# Only languages that are *active* in Odoo can be asked for — an inactive code
# is an error, not a fallback — so the build reads `res.lang` and falls back to
# en_US. Activating nl_BE and fr_BE in Odoo is all it takes for translated
# vacancies to reach the site; nothing here changes.
#
# In production these are Cloudflare Pages *build* variables, and ODOO_API_KEY
# is marked as a secret. They are never Function bindings and never reach the
# browser: the build calls Odoo, and what ships is the job text.
# `scripts/check-dist.mjs` fails the build if the value lands in `dist/`.
ODOO_LOGIN=
ODOO_API_KEY=

# Defaults are correct for production; set only against another database.
# ODOO_ORIGIN=https://smartagents.odoo.com
# ODOO_DB=smartagents

# Skip the network and render the committed snapshot instead. `npm run dev`
# sets this on its own; put it here only to make every local build offline.
# ODOO_OFFLINE=1
